                <pb facs="1318" n="1312" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1312"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you of the arrival in this
                    port, on the 22d of this month, of the Japanese man-of-war <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Takachiho</hi>. The Japanese man-of-war <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Naniwa</hi> returned from the island of Hawaii the same
                    day. The <hi rendition="#italic">Takachiho</hi> carries 360 men and officers,
                    and has the following armament: Two 26-centimeter Krupp guns, 6 15-centimeter
                    Krupp guns, 2 47-millimeter quick-firing guns, 10 1-inch Wordenfeldt, and 4
                    Gatling guns. She has 4 torpedo tubes.</p>
                <p>The officer in command, Capt. T. Nomura, during his official call on the 23d
                    instantiated that he expected to remain here several months.</p>
                <p>With high esteem, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
